{"reference":"Psalms 147","book":"Psalms","chapter":147,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"Psalm Numbering","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"Readers comparing Psalm numbers across traditions may find a difference here. Greek and Latin Psalters divide Psalm 147, while the Masoretic tradition presents it as one psalm. This is part of a broader numbering difference caused by some psalms being combined or divided differently in these traditions.","verse_refs":["Psalms 147:1-20"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_psalms_147_9d8e9a7bbb5d6d47910f5f59"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]},{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"Among the Closing Psalms","blocks":[{"id":"block_2","text":"Psalm 147 belongs to the Psalter’s closing sequence of praise in Psalms 146–150. In the Masoretic Psalter, these five psalms form the concluding crescendo of an anthology arranged in five books.","verse_refs":["Psalms 146:1-10","Psalms 148:1-14","Psalms 149:1-9","Psalms 150:1-6"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_psalms_147_703a0ed0564a71be6ae316f7"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}